{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1431867-core-initial-enhancements-in-a-complex-actions","id":1431867,"title":"[Core] Initial Enhancements in a Complex Actions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-11T13:20:33-08:00","id":1431867,"title":"[Core] Initial Enhancements in a Complex Actions","content":"I have a question about how to proceed when there are initial Enhancements in a Complex Action.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <i>A computer programmer needs to create extremely complex and advanced software, and this task will take several rounds (or days), being an Extended Complex Action with 4 milestones. The programmer has \u201cspecialized equipment\u201d that gives him +2 enhancements.</i><br /> <br /> Remembering that:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cIf a player rolls more successes than he needs to complete a milestone, he creates an Enhancement for his next roll attempt. This kind of Enhancement costs two successes to create. \u201d (Trinity Continuum Core Pag. 77) </div> </div> </div>My question is: Is the \u201cspecialized equipment\u201d Enhancement valid on EACH milestone? Like that.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=898\" data-tempid=\"temp_898_1610399808912_270\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> ...or is the \u201cspecialized equipment\u201d Enhancement used only at the beginning of the Complex Action (first milestone)? Like that.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=899\" data-tempid=\"temp_899_1610399834101_466\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T14:01:06-08:00","id":1431874,"title":"","content":"pretty sure that it applies to all applicable milestones. It may not apply to planning, or resource acquisition (that may be more Aberrant), but for most of the milestones it would likely apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T14:18:59-08:00","id":1431877,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and remember all milestones don't have to be the same action. The first milestone could be planning the program, which may not count as applicable for specialized equipment, for example. It depends what the equipment is and if it can be used on any particular milestone's action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T15:02:42-08:00","id":1431882,"title":"","content":"I modeled the example as a Complex Action Extended, which according to the book is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cA task that takes a long period of time. She divides the task into two or more milestones and rolls the same dice pool for each milestone. The milestones occur in sequence. (Trinity Continuum Core Pag. 78)\u201d </div> </div> </div>In this case, the dice pool is the same.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T16:12:38-08:00","id":1431894,"title":"","content":"Then yes, it would be applicable for each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T05:30:31-08:00","id":1431954,"title":"","content":"Although, I might argue you should use the super-science rules if it's going to be software beyond what is currently available. That would let you have various kinds of actions for the creation instead of the same roll for every milestone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T11:11:39-08:00","id":1431985,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I thought it was a super-science question...If it is complex normal tech, then it would apply to all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T14:03:53-08:00","id":1432002,"title":"","content":"Regular tech can be created as a complex action if it improves the game, for example coding something to disable the security system while it attacks the team, but regular tech don\u2019t have all the other need the super science items have, like special materials and long milestones.<br /> <br /> Honestly I would change the difficulties of Superscience creation to 3 Ranks 1 or 2, 4 ranks 3 and 4, 5 ranks 5 and 6, and so on, so regular tech would have difficulty 1, maybe 2 for the most complex regular tech. The number of milestones stay the same, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}